    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/content-context-and-state-graphs.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Content, context and state graphs",
      "prov:value": "An instance declares directories, and each says what **kind** of graph it\nholds. Until 2026-09-20 a kind answered one question — does this render as a\nwebsite — and a consumer had no way to tell the subject matter from a record\nabout it, or a record it may write from one it may not.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/content-context-and-state-graphs.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "One question settles every kind",
      "prov:value": "**`content`'s example used to be \"a library section\" and that was wrong** —\nsee §\"The case that added `derived`\" below. It is a folio chapter now."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/content-context-and-state-graphs.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The classification",
      "prov:value": "Ask the code, not this page — `graphTypologiesOfLayer(\"context\")` returns the live\nanswer. **No count appears here on purpose**: a count in prose is a claim\nnothing checks, and this repository has corrected two of them."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/content-context-and-state-graphs.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The classification",
      "prov:value": "**`memory` is `context`, and it is the kind the third layer was added for.**\nThe owner, settling bean `mhh9`, 2026-09-20:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean mhh9",
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/content-context-and-state-graphs.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The classification",
      "prov:value": "**`fsh-guts` is `context`, and it is the one that reads like content.** It\nholds structured material that *could* be rendered — which is what makes it\nhard — and the fact it carries is *where something got to*: abandoned,\nsuperseded, decided against. But **no running step writes it**. Relocating\nsomething there is a human-directed act, and\n[`deletion-requires-confirmation`](../../conduct/conduct-core/deletion-requires-confirmation.md) is the\nskill that says so in as many words. Read, never written by a process. It was\n`state` for the few hours between the axis landing and `mhh9` being settled,\nand the refinement moved it by the same criterion that moved memory."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/content-context-and-state-graphs.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The classification",
      "prov:value": "**`attestations` is `state` too, and it is the half of `qa` that stays on\n`main`.** Arc `3fva` split every QA verdict by whether it can be regenerated.\nThe DERIVED half (`qa`, and `health` with it) is state a CI run writes, and\nits record now lives on the orphan `qa-reports` branch keyed by commit — the\ncheckout's `test/results/` is a working copy, still committed until bean\n`5hox` removes it. The JUDGEMENT half — agent, human and baseline-pair\nattestations, `qa-attestations/v1` under `test/attestations/` — is written by\na review step too, so it is `state` by the same question, but it is the one\nstate graph here that **cannot be rebuilt by re-running its writer**. That is\nwhy it stays on `main` (owner ruling D2 (a)) and why a merge conflict in it\nis a person's to read rather than a generator's to repeat. The layer answers\n*who writes it*; where it is kept answers *can it be reproduced* — two\nquestions, and the arc is what made the second one visible."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/content-context-and-state-graphs.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where each layer lives",
      "prov:value": "| layer (`holds`) | example | default ref | keyed by | write shape |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `content` | chapters, skills, processes | `main` | — | PR |\n| `context` | interaction prefs, roles | `main` | — | PR |\n| `state` | beans, workflow instances, todos | dedicated branch-store branches (e.g. `cat/cat-harness/beans`, `cat/cat-harness/todos`) | **tip** — one living tree | fetch → splice → push, never `-f` |\n| `derived` (verdicts) | QA sidecars | `cat/cat-harness/qa-reports` (arc 3fva) | commit | append under `main/<sha>/`, `pr/<n>/<sha>/` |\n| rendered | the docs site | `gh-pages` | commit (the build stamp) | replace, previews kept |\n| cache | Lake builds | `lake-cache/*` | toolchain + inputs | one key per branch, pruned |"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/content-context-and-state-graphs.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "`route` is not a synonym for `tip`, and the difference is REGENERABILITY",
      "prov:value": "Both live at a branch tip, so the temptation is to read them as one keying with\ntwo names. The question that separates them is the one §3.1 of the state-branch\nproposal already asks: **can this be recomputed from the tree?**"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/content-context-and-state-graphs.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "`route` is not a synonym for `tip`, and the difference is REGENERABILITY",
      "prov:value": "Four rules (bean `2h76`, owner rulings 2026-10-02; `route` from bean `1j3q`,\nowner 2026-10-03 — *\"Add route-keyed storage, then move it off main\"*):",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 2h76",
        "bean 1j3q",
        "2026-10-02",
        "2026-10-03"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-02",
        "2026-10-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/content-context-and-state-graphs.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "`route` is not a synonym for `tip`, and the difference is REGENERABILITY",
      "prov:value": "A branch-tip read is **hit / miss / corrupt / unknown**, and a branch without a\n`state-manifest/v1` root manifest is `corrupt`, not a hit — for a route-keyed\nbranch too. The `$schema` string says `state-manifest` on both, and that is a\nchoice: the two seeded branches already carry it, the format is identical in\nevery field, and `keyedBy` **inside** the manifest is the discriminator, which\nis this repository's own rule that the file declares what it is. The name is\nhistorical; bean `1j3q` records it as such. A write is spliced\nonto the tip and pushed **without `-f`**, retrying when the tip moves. To edit\na file somebody else may be editing, pass the blob you read as `expect`. A tip\nthat disagrees then answers `conflict` and pushes nothing, so the edit is not\nsilently lost.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 1j3q"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/content-context-and-state-graphs.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "`route` is not a synonym for `tip`, and the difference is REGENERABILITY",
      "prov:value": "**Until a declaration sets `storage`, `main` is authoritative.** That holds for\n`route` too: no generator writes a route-keyed branch yet, and the first family\n(`docs/uml/`) is a follow-on bean to `1j3q` — deliberately separate, because 49\nof 94 gated checks write page files and a flip of all of them cannot be\nbisected. A directory\nwith no `storage` field lives in the checkout, whatever branches exist. The\nseeded `cat/cat-harness/beans` and `cat/cat-harness/todos` say\n`authoritative: false` in their manifests until the steward-run flip on #1850.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1850"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/content-context-and-state-graphs.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Adding a kind",
      "prov:value": "## The case that added `derived` — `library/`, 2026-09-20",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/content-context-and-state-graphs.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The case that added `derived` — `library/`, 2026-09-20",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-09-20: *\"library is static (only if we materialize assets or\nnot)\"* and *\"can duplicate asset into a folio and work there.\"* Bean `hqku`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean hqku",
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/content-context-and-state-graphs.md#provenance-14",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Classifying a kind is not a ruling on a directory's contents",
      "prov:value": "`cat-harness` is correctly `content`. For a few hours on 2026-09-20,\n`skills/memory/` sat inside a `cat-harness` directory and held `context`.\n**Both were true at once**, and that is the case that shows why the two\nquestions are separate: classifying a kind says what that KIND holds, not what\nevery node beneath a directory of that kind is.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/content-context-and-state-graphs.md#provenance-15",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The layer is not the source — a branch is not \"where state lives\"",
      "prov:value": "A declared subgraph also says where its content COMES FROM — the checkout's\ndirectory or a declared repository branch, overridable by the instance config\n(`source`, [`directory-conventions`](directory-conventions.md) §\"Where a\nsubgraph gets its content\"; bean `l4ay`). **That is a different axis from this\none, and neither is derived from the other.**",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean l4ay"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/content-context-and-state-graphs.md#provenance-16",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "A declared ASSET carries a layer too",
      "prov:value": "The axis is not only about directories. `instance-readme` and\n`agent-instructions` are declared assets, and both hold **`context`** — the\nowner's own words on issue #592: *\"its static content at process runtime and\ntreated as an asset like memories\"*. `README.md` and `AGENTS.md` are read at\nsession start and authored by a human, so a step that rewrites one is a defect\nby the same rule a step writing to `memory/` is.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#592"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/content-context-and-state-graphs.md#provenance-17",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "A declared ASSET carries a layer too",
      "prov:value": "**Creation at INITIALISATION is not a process write.** A `context` asset that\ndoes not exist yet has to come from somewhere, and bootstrap writing one when\nit is absent is not the write this rule forbids: **initialisation is not\nprocess runtime.** `initialize-harness.bpmn` ends with `A_WriteRootReadme`\n(`bootstrap/skills/root-readme.md`), which writes the root `README.md` when\nthere is none and **never replaces** one that exists — an existing README is\nauthored content, and the link and install status go in a marker pair that\n`readme_sync` owns from then on (bean `7sfm`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 7sfm"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/content-context-and-state-graphs.md#provenance-18",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "See also",
      "prov:value": "- [`directory-conventions`](directory-conventions.md) — what a declaration is\n  and how a path resolves. This page is the axis; that one is the mechanism.\n- [`agent-memory`](../../conduct/conduct-core/agent-memory.md) — what a memory entry promises, and the\n  injection budget. This page says what layer it is on.\n- [`process-state`](../../process/workflow/process-state.md), [`bpmn-processes`](../../process/workflow/bpmn-processes.md) —\n  the largest writer of a live-state graph: a workflow instance is a token's\n  position in a diagram that lives in a content graph.\n- [`todo-manager`](../../../work-plan/skills/work-plan/todo-manager.md), [`bean-coordination`](../../../work-plan/skills/work-plan/bean-coordination.md)\n  — the work plan, and why a bean is never deleted. A state record that\n  vanishes leaves a sibling unable to tell abandonment from accident.\n- [`instance-publication`](instance-publication.md#what-each-instance-publishes--graph-address-schema-and-what-is-stripped)\n  — a `state` graph's nodes are never published. That rule, and every other\n  rule about what reaches the site, lives there (bean `4ak5` item 4).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 4ak5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/content-context-and-state-graphs.md#provenance-19",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Classifying a kind is not a ruling on a directory's contents",
      "prov:value": "The nodes have since moved to their own declared `memory/` graph (bean\n`07xs`), as their own change — relocating a directory as a side effect of\nadding a classification is the shape #395 refused and bean `auap` did\nseparately. So the example is now history rather than a live gap, and it is\nkept because the rule it illustrates is not: **a directory of one kind may\ncontain a node of another, and the containing declaration is not a claim about\nits contents.**",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 07xs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/content-context-and-state-graphs.md#provenance-20",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "A declared ASSET carries a layer too",
      "prov:value": "**A process may CREATE or REPAIR the declaration (`<name>.json`) or config\n(`<name>.config.json`). It never maintains it.** Every `state` graph is one a\nrunning process keeps current (beans, QA witnesses, workflow tokens). Neither\n`<name>.json` nor `<name>.config.json` is that: `init-folio` writes them once\nwhen there is no folio yet, and `ensure-landing-sticky` inserts one missing\n`folio` directory entry on `!already` and returns on `already` thereafter — a\none-time repair, never ongoing state maintenance (bean `b5f0`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean b5f0"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
